  "title": "Investigating Persistence Mechanisms in AWS",
  "summary": "In the cloud, your infrastructure may be short-lived, but an attacker’s persistence may not be. While your environment scales and changes in seconds, adversaries are embedding themselves into your IAM policies, Lambda functions, and federated sessions – creating invisible footholds that survive long after you believe an incident is closed.",
